A||||34||stsmithgt||I just got tagged in the passenger side.:(||||8||
Z||000000||stsmithgt||01-22-2001||05:59 PM||||Well folks, At lunch I got tagged in the side by a big rental car.  Some punk was driving it and said he didn't see me.  I was taking a left turn, with a left turn arrow light, The coast was clear enough for me to make it through the intersection almost clear through the cross walk.  That's when I felt a large impact that knocked me sideways and headed me up over a big curb with my brand new tires on! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  The punk said he was distracted by some lady in front of him.?  His brain must process info pretty slow because the intersection was clear when I went through.  No Mercedes was blocking my path.  Anyway, my car got hauled off the the door smashed shut, front suspension bent and a scratched up brand freakin' new sail panel I just put on a few days ago.  He hit my car right on the door hinge and left a tire mark in the middle of my door.  Here's the part that dropped my jaw..  An old lady said that I ran into HIM! what?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  Since I didn't see the guy plow into me, and he said he didn't see me,  they lady's fu**** story had weight for the police.  I'm being SCREWED by an old lady that doesn't know whos coming and whos going. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  The one day I don't have my camera on me!  I'm totally depressed after all the money I've put into this car.  I know some you out there know how I feel. *sniff*  I was told to get a lawyer.  That is next on my list of things to do once my allready bad back stops spazzing out on me.  My car is in getting an estimate right now. $$$$.$$ Hope everyone else has a better day than this.  Talk to ya later.      Todd Smith (separated from his GT) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   ||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-22-2001||06:31 PM||||Damn, that sucks the big one.  Stupid old people, I've got plenty of old fart stories and how not-smart they are.  <P>Hope it all comes out, I know how depressed I would be if something happend to my car with all the work that is put into it.<P>Damn teenage drivers.....<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||9
Z||000002||fropuff||01-22-2001||06:40 PM||||How could you run into him when he smashed the sh*t out of your passenger side?  Maybe if you were doing a side-steer, it could be possible.  Might want to take pictures of the site.  Your new tires will help too.  They will have horizontal gouges on them; and the skid marks will show as well that he pushed you.  You should go and punch that old lady right in the nose, in my opinion.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||01-22-2001||07:42 PM||||I can feel your pain (and back spasms).  Just last weekend I had some idiot spin out in the lane next to me and end up sideways across both lanes of trafic right infront of me.  Needless to say I smashed right into his side with my dads 87 SC.  Its repairable, and in fact I just got home with a pickup truck full of Fiero parts of a junked car to rebuild it with!  Good luck with the ins. co!  They are bigger bastards than the idiot drivers!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||01-22-2001||07:58 PM||||That old lady was lucky I didn't have my .45 in my door pocket. J/k sorta.... My new tires do have some serious scrub on them.  I was surprized the officer asked how I got up on the sidewalk.  I explained to him how my car got pushed sideways, but he was treating me more like a criminal than a victom of an accident.  I was shocked at his attitude.  He didn't really want to hear what I had to say.  My don't think my appearance is threatening either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00069.jpg">  (goofball)I even had the same shirt on today. I'm going to go get my camera as soon as I get off this computor.  I was just checking for responces while I picked up some stuff out of my car I had sitting on my work bench.  I'm having to wait for a couple of calls from the claim dept. and my cars estimate before my next move.  (Taking that info to a lawyer) My back and neck are killing me in more places than what was almost normal.  So much for sleep tonight.  I'll post any major changes in my situation so everyone can be more enlightened in what could happen to anyone. My poor gt. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000005||JBGehling||01-22-2001||08:56 PM||||whoah! There seems to have been a good deal of fiero wrecks recently and the fiero seems to ALWAYS be at fault (someone pulled right out in front of me and a witness said I swerved off the road and hit the car)! I hope you'll have as much luck as I did with the time ahead... <BR>The estimate given to my car was $4500, but it's only going to cost a local car restoration shop 3200 thanks to the large amount of fiero shops on the net. That means I just made 1300 dollars for that and they're paying me 25 dollars a day until the car gets fixed (they're going to pay me for about 3 weeks) for the daily rental car fees (I've been driving the formula). There's $525 more dollars. For a grand total of $1825 I made out of this wreck (of course, my fiero will never be factory perfect again... just stock perfect  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)  I didn't pay a penny of this (the insurance company investigated this wreck and they decided the girl was totally at fault.) My insurance didn't go up, and there was no ticket issued!<P>Good Luck, <BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000006||RaeQwan||01-22-2001||09:14 PM||||Well luckily when the 'old' fart backed into my 88.. I had a witness that lives with me, my brother was in his car sitting right behind me. older drivers, in this case 70(with a restriction), should have more restrictions on their license, like, if you see a fiero around, pull to the side of the road and stay till it leaves the area .. hehe..<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwansig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||01-22-2001||10:57 PM||||I would think that if you had a turn arrow, that the rental must have run the light. I find it hard to believe that you hit some body with the side of your car and then got pushed up onto the sidewalk!<BR>Get back to the accident site and take many pictures of the scene as you can!<BR>Also pay attention to the light sequencing, I've seen it aroud in many places that the left turn arrow is still on when the oncoming traffic signal goes to green! If that may be the case, then determine whose responsible for the light (city or state) and report it! A friend looking from the other direction would help to see light changing, time the interval if it's off, and get a copy of the repair order or try to get photos of the repair in progress!<BR>Since the other driver was 'distracted' by some lady in front of him (?), he really doesn't know WTF happened at all! So far as the 'witness' goes, what was her vantage point? Perhaps the 'distraction'?<P>I don't understand your statement about the intersection though:<P>'The coast was clear enough for me to make it through the intersection almost clear through the cross walk.'<P> How far was it to the curb anyway? What is the posted speed limit in the area? For you to have a turn arrow, makes sense that your oncoming traffic needed to be stopped or at least real slow! If the impact was hard enough with the sort of momentum  needed to put a Fiero over a curb, sounds like someone was speeding or was just in a plain F*CKIN' hurry and was playing in his pants at the same time!<BR>Gather your info and take it to your insurance company they should help in the legalities unless the just like to pay out!<P>LUCK!<BR>         <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Notchit||01-22-2001||11:05 PM||||Aww man, sorry to hear....that makes me mad, when people are careless, but I am also one of those teenage drivers, so were not all bad. I have to admit though, some kids have no brains....good luck with the repairs.<P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Outside_side2(sml2).jpg"> <BR>_________________________||||reg||4
Z||000009||frontal lobe||01-23-2001||01:36 AM||||You must have quite a case of oversteer to be whipping around and putting the smackdown on people with your passenger door!<P>I am so sorry for what happened, and then all the hassle, too.<P>You must have a white GT.  Those white cars sure are hard to see...||||reg||1
Z||000010||stsmithgt||01-23-2001||09:18 AM||||'The coast was clear enough for me to make it through the intersection almost clear through the cross walk.'<P>What I meant was, the intersection was clear.  I had a clear path.  I got hit when I was almost through the cross walk at the end of my turn.  I was practicaly pointed straight down the road I was turning on to when I got hit, which was while I was passing through the cross walk.  Not the cross walk I was stopped at waiting for the light.  The pain I felt yesterday didn't go away so I'm going to the doctor today.  Oh well I'll see what goes on today besides getting more pictures with better lighting today.||||reg||9
Z||000011||HAGS||01-23-2001||10:21 AM||||If you were in the crosswalk of the next street then the cop should have given the guy a ticket for wreckless driving or assault with a deadly weapon...why would he pull off his street to hit you in the side of another?  And im pretty sure green arrow gives you right of way, but was it a left turn yield on green kind of street?  I almost got in an accident just like this the other day.  I was going through a regular green light and this car turns left even though he is supposed to yeild...of course my accelerator decides to stick and im hitting the brakes and still screaming towards him, I throw it in nuetral and skid into the left lane as he passes through the intersection...had to miss him by less than a foot...||||reg||1
Z||000012||fieroshop||01-23-2001||10:49 AM||||Todd, sorry to hear you got run into. If thee is anything we can do to help, call me.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000013||stsmithgt||01-23-2001||11:31 AM||||Thanks guys.  He would have to hit about where the door hinges are.  I'm getting an estimate on the damages and maybe they can see if the frame is bent up too badly.  I'll let you know FieroShop.  I'm still trying to figure out how he hit me so hard to put a tire mark on the door and still throw me sideways up over the curb with all 4 tires.  I suppose it being a full size car is enough to toss around a little Fiero.  I didn't get over to the body shop soon enough yesterday to get pictures, but I'm going today.  I'll post some sad pictures.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Indiana_resto_guy||01-23-2001||03:18 PM||||Sounds almost like he was making a right hand turn to the same street you were turning to? Since you were already committed and established within the intersection and almost clear, he must have been gawking at a babe on the corner(his distraction) and didn't see you because he wasn't paying attention and didn't know if hes path was clear as a result!<BR>Let' see . . . rental car . . . .is he from the area or from else where? People not famaliar with an area should pay closer attention to what they're doing instead of enjoying the view(s)! (statement to use with the insurance company)||||reg||1
Z||000015||stsmithgt||01-23-2001||05:35 PM||||I hope this works and isn't to big.       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hit3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hit2.jpg">    <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hit1.jpg">   <BR>The pictures don't make it look that bad, but it looks like I put a lowering kit on that corner of the car.  It was close to a wall at the bodyshop so I couldn't get a broad view.  They haven't given me an estimate yet, but they're already talking about when I'm going to get that totaled car out of there when I went to get the pictures today. geeeez.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 01-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||tgowens||01-23-2001||09:17 PM||||if the insurance co. totals your car does that mean that I will finally get that steering wheel??? - really, that is a real shame Todd - it is obvious from the pictures that you didn't hit that guy - the evidence will illustrate that no matter what the little ol' lady said (she was probably the guys mother - did you notice her getting out of his car???)............too bad you didn't have your lucky frogs with you!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Indiana_resto_guy||01-24-2001||12:24 AM||||I'll be honest about it!<BR>I've restored LOTS worse than that. If they total it, look into buying it back. Without getting under it looks like a right front fender, right side door skin, right rear quarter panel right front lower control arm (w/ball joint), inner and outer tie rod ends and a possible upper control arm. (maybe a door frame, that depends on internal damage) Not all that bad.||||reg||1
Z||000018||stsmithgt||01-24-2001||10:15 AM||||Oh Terry,,,, Your toooooooooo funny.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">......That's a thought.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00110.jpg">  would that be a squished door or bent frame? I only had liability on it.  If it's totaled, I expect them to drop it off at my door step.  I don't think they value these cars so it wouldn't take much for them to total it.  Then it comes down to how much money would it take to fix it.  Or sell it to someone with the interest to fix it.  I've got enough money to just go buy another, but just the thought after putting thousands into this one makes me sick.  So the question if it comes to that.  Will I fix mine or go get another one??  Or get a monster truck and start running over a bunch of people in a shopping mall parking lot???*slap!* *slap* *slap* SNAP OUT OF IT! AHhhh. That's better.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Anyway, I think the pain killers are kicking in.  I'd better get back to work.  talk to you later.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
